      "content": "That's a good start, but I need to get a bit more granular for the \"counter-history\" aspect of my essay. To really understand how they justified it as a \"stabilizer,\" I need to look at the more \"scientific\" or sociological claims they made back then. \n\nCould you expand on the arguments regarding \"social friction\" or \"cultural incompatibility\"? Specifically, how did they use things like sociology or even biological theories at the time to argue that integration would lead to inevitable chaos or the breakdown of the social fabric? I'm trying to see how they used \"logic\" to make these ideas sound like legitimate policy rather than just prejudice.",
